      "css": ".ds-ability{display:grid;justify-items:center;gap:6px;border:1px solid #6f5a45;border-radius:3px;padding:10px;background:#f3e8cf;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 3px #f3e8cf,inset 0 0 0 4px #b79f74}.ds-ability h4{margin:0;color:#5a4535;font:700 .72rem/1.2 ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-mod{display:grid;width:64px;height:64px;place-items:center;border:3px double #8f6b34;border-radius:50%;color:#2a1c13;background:#f3e8cf;font:600 1.7rem/1 \"Source Serif 4\",Georgia,serif}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Journal Toast",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "journal-toast",
      "description": "Leather note with a lantern mark, brass border, and dismiss button.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-toast\"><span class=\"ds-mark\"></span><span>Sheet saved.</span><button type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Dismiss notification\">×</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-toast{display:flex;min-height:44px;align-items:center;gap:10px;border:2px solid #dab98a;border-radius:3px;padding:4px 4px 4px 12px;color:#fff0d7;background:#221310;box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgb(11 9 18 / .5);font:600 .92rem/1.35 ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-mark{width:8px;height:8px;background:#f2b04a}.ds-toast button{min-width:36px;min-height:36px;border:0;color:#fff0d7;background:transparent;font-size:1.2rem}.ds-toast button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ffe7ac;outline-offset:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Adventure Ledger",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Adventure Ledger\"**\n\nA calm, personal player record for quick use during and between sessions. The visual language takes the form of a contemporary player handbook spread: warm uncoated paper, charcoal serif display type, narrow folio rules, and restrained oxblood accents.\n\nThe mood is a personal campaign journal with softer earth tones and lightly lifted sections. Familiar web controls stay clear and central; the forms share equal weight and stack in reading order on small screens.\n\nThe ledger now has three rooms that share one ink and one accent. Sign-in and account pages are the **plain ledger**: light paper, charcoal ink, oxblood folios. The campaign galaxy and the camp are **night scenes**: midnight violet chrome with starlight and brass. Everything a player reads or edits inside the camp (Overview, Party, Campaign settings, My characters, the character sheet) is the **adventurer's journal**: a leather cover around parchment pages, with brass fittings and a lantern accent. Oxblood runs through all three; the journal is where the ledger became a physical book.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper and charcoal ink establish a quiet reading surface; in the journal the same role is played by parchment and brown-black ink.",
      "Serif display type and sans-serif interface text balance print character with quick scanning.",
      "Oxblood folios mark primary actions and active routes; supporting colors stay tied to states.",
      "Light paper panels receive a restrained lift, and form controls remain conventional.",
      "The journal's controls are tactile (pressed-key buttons, double-ruled plates, dashed stitching) but always at least 44px and always labelled in words.",
      "Small pixel icons, drawn in one weight, mark places and states; they never replace a label."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Oxblood Folio Rule",
        "body": "Use oxblood for the main route and action cues; keep focus blue and success green tied to their specific states.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Rooms Rule",
        "body": "Plain paper, night scene, and journal each keep their own tokens. Do not carry a journal color onto the auth pages, or a `--camp-*` color onto parchment.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Words Beside Color Rule",
        "body": "Status chips, save state, and errors always pair color with an icon and words.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Is For Names Rule",
        "body": "Titles, character names, and numerals take the serif. Labels, buttons, hints, and anything a player edits take the sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Lift Rule",
        "body": "Keep the shadow on the auth panel and let paper contrast and rules do the remaining work on plain pages.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Plate Not Card Rule",
        "body": "Group parchment content with a double rule, a divider, or a ribbon, not nested rounded cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep sign-in and account creation equally weighted in the current auth layout.",
      "**Do** retain standard labeled fields, visible keyboard focus, and clear text states.",
      "**Do** stack the account panels in reading order on small screens.",
      "**Do** reserve the panel shadow for the auth panel and use paper tones and rules for surrounding structure.",
      "**Do** keep camp colours in `--camp-*` tokens, journal colours in `--journal-*` tokens, and status text in always-mounted live regions.",
      "**Do** build new camp pages from `CampPanel` and the `journal-*` primitives (button, field, input, section title, chip, status, alert) so they inherit the cover, parchment, and 44px targets.",
      "**Do** pair every status color with an icon and words, and keep touch targets at 44px or more in the journal.",
      "**Do** put a destructive action behind an inline confirmation in the dashed oxblood zone."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** turn standard form controls into decorative props.",
      "**Don't** let fantasy ornament or surface decoration compete with the form labels and actions.",
      "**Don't** use the focus and success colors as general-purpose accents.",
      "**Don't** let camp name plates or scene art carry information the Places list and the journal do not also provide.",
      "**Don't** put a journal skin (leather, brass, parchment) on the auth pages or the galaxy.",
      "**Don't** nest plates inside plates, or use the pressed-key shadow outside buttons.",
      "**Don't** use Lantern as a fill or for large areas; it is a small warm signal."
    ]
  }
}